WEBVTT

00:05.430 --> 00:06.760
Don’t worry.

00:07.630 --> 00:10.400
We, and you, will all be able to leave.

00:11.300 --> 00:12.550
Why?

00:13.100 --> 00:14.290
Well...

00:17.630 --> 00:20.030
The power to create miracles...

00:20.980 --> 00:24.050
If I told you that, would you believe me?

00:43.450 --> 00:46.320
<i>From today on, I’ll be able to study here.</i>

00:47.500 --> 00:50.130
<i>To study the same power they had...</i>

01:10.330 --> 01:12.930
Cherry blossoms in fall?

01:26.900 --> 01:27.980
What?

01:29.300 --> 01:35.370
Um... Well... So pretty...

01:39.790 --> 01:42.660
The cherry blossoms...

01:46.490 --> 01:48.750
What are you?

01:49.650 --> 01:51.560
What am I?

01:51.560 --> 01:53.520
Who are you? Which class?

01:53.520 --> 01:54.310
Oh!

01:54.310 --> 01:56.510
Yoshimura Mamoru, Basics Class 2.

02:05.140 --> 02:06.890
Excuse me.

02:08.240 --> 02:10.290
Here you go! I got it.

02:14.040 --> 02:15.080
Hey!

02:15.830 --> 02:20.260
You need to... t-t-to...

02:20.260 --> 02:20.880
Need to?

02:20.880 --> 02:22.540
Be my boyfriend!

02:34.380 --> 02:35.960
OK...

02:39.000 --> 02:40.280
Did you hear?

02:39.570 --> 02:46.340
Beatrice in Love

02:40.280 --> 02:42.940
Yeah. Takasu Ayako asked someone out!

02:42.940 --> 02:43.730
No way!

02:43.730 --> 02:44.690
Who? Who?

02:44.690 --> 02:47.350
They say it’s a freshman who just transferred!

02:47.350 --> 02:48.670
I can’t believe it...

02:48.670 --> 02:50.350
Witch Beatrice, asking someone out?

02:50.350 --> 02:52.510
You’re being too loud!

02:50.350 --> 02:51.730
Student Council

02:50.350 --> 02:51.730
Meeting
In Progress.

02:52.510 --> 02:56.570
If she hears you, you’d be stripped naked and hanged from the Wind Bell tower.

02:58.280 --> 03:00.070
This is a major problem.

03:00.070 --> 03:03.420
Topic: Attempted Lab Support Infiltration

03:00.070 --> 03:03.410
We don’t have time for minor issues like this.

03:04.090 --> 03:08.250
Everyone, the coming battle will demand
that we risk our very lives.

03:08.830 --> 03:10.230
Do you understand?

03:10.230 --> 03:12.130
Of course.

03:16.550 --> 03:19.280
Takasu-sempai asked you out?

03:19.280 --> 03:21.050
Oh, sorry.

03:21.050 --> 03:23.940
But man, your cheeks are really squishy.

03:23.940 --> 03:27.120
Thanks. I, uh, guess.

03:28.300 --> 03:32.960
Anyway, so Beatrice’s Angel of Death
is in love with you, huh?

03:32.960 --> 03:34.620
Look over there.

03:35.560 --> 03:36.600
And in the hallway.

03:41.440 --> 03:44.200
They’re all really interested in you,

03:44.200 --> 03:46.700
but they’re too scared of Takasu-sempai to get close.

03:46.700 --> 03:49.880
Is she that scary?

03:49.880 --> 03:52.790
She’s pretty, but she’s ice-cold.

03:52.790 --> 03:54.580
No one’s ever seen her smile.

03:54.580 --> 03:56.290
Smile?

03:57.350 --> 03:59.670
She heads the Student Council’s Security Group.

03:59.670 --> 04:02.520
Her job’s supposedly to settle school fights.

04:02.520 --> 04:05.050
But she’s way more powerful than that.

04:05.050 --> 04:09.290
They say the government once asked
her to take out an American spy satellite.

04:11.060 --> 04:14.030
And another time, during the
Sea Line Wars two years ago,

04:14.030 --> 04:17.570
she took out an entire division alone.

04:22.440 --> 04:26.920
Th-Those are some rather big rumors.

04:26.920 --> 04:30.870
So ya scared now, Yoshimura Mamoru?

04:35.330 --> 04:36.880
Abiko-sempai?

04:36.880 --> 04:39.260
Watanabe-kun, who’s this?

04:39.750 --> 04:44.090
Takasu-sempai’s stalker...
No, fan... No, follower...

04:44.090 --> 04:46.930
No... Captain of her bodyguards!

04:46.930 --> 04:48.100
Not that she’s ever called him that.

04:48.710 --> 04:52.200
That’s what’s wrong with you morons.

04:52.200 --> 04:55.600
Don’t you know that love’s at its
most splendid when it’s hidden?

04:55.600 --> 04:57.400
I see...

04:58.530 --> 05:00.210
Speaking of which, Yoshimura Mamoru,

05:00.210 --> 05:05.870
are you prepared to give up your life for Ayako-san?

05:05.870 --> 05:07.700
M-My life?

05:07.700 --> 05:12.140
Her beatrice-control level is
a matter of national security!

05:12.140 --> 05:15.750
To love her means...

05:18.120 --> 05:19.930
Nice face shot.

05:20.500 --> 05:21.920
Hi there.

05:21.920 --> 05:23.760
I’m Fujita Mitsuki.

05:23.760 --> 05:25.270
Hi, I’m...

05:25.270 --> 05:28.430
You can take your time introducing yourself later.

05:28.430 --> 05:31.410
If I’m the only one to enjoy it,
everyone else will get mad.

05:31.410 --> 05:32.470
Everyone else?

05:32.840 --> 05:34.610
Let’s go.

05:35.960 --> 05:37.080
Wait!

05:37.080 --> 05:39.230
Are you going to run, Yoshimura?

05:39.230 --> 05:39.970
We’re not done talking—

05:39.970 --> 05:40.510
Here you go!

05:42.400 --> 05:43.780
What are these?

05:45.470 --> 05:50.700
Ayako-san ch-ch-ch-changing?!

05:51.090 --> 05:53.570
My sweet honey baby!

05:53.570 --> 05:56.130
I’m so happy!

06:07.730 --> 06:09.170
Welcome.

06:09.780 --> 06:14.250
The Student Council welcomes you,
Yoshimura Mamoru-kun.

06:14.250 --> 06:15.850
Come in.

06:15.850 --> 06:17.460
Oh, OK.

06:22.520 --> 06:24.440
Hello, everyone...

06:24.440 --> 06:25.320
Um...

06:25.320 --> 06:28.450
I’m the Student Council President, Sudou Maya.

06:28.450 --> 06:31.070
I’ve heard the rumors.

06:31.070 --> 06:34.740
You volunteered for the second JBA
Preliminary Examination,

06:34.740 --> 06:37.530
passing with a recognized Beatrice Sympathy ability.

06:38.140 --> 06:42.510
Your BCMA test result was seventh
highest in school history.

06:43.260 --> 06:45.380
A-Amazing...

06:45.380 --> 06:48.950
I can see why Ayako was so impressed.

06:48.950 --> 06:51.000
Yeah, really...

06:51.000 --> 06:54.850
I guess you’d have to be so good, to be a match

06:54.850 --> 06:57.630
for that lethal weapon of a woman.

06:59.030 --> 07:00.210
I’m sorry.

07:00.210 --> 07:02.210
Let’s get to the point.

07:02.210 --> 07:03.290
Shione?

07:03.290 --> 07:04.470
All right.

07:05.930 --> 07:08.700
Emergency

07:15.860 --> 07:18.830
Topic: Takasu Ayako’s First Love,
Operation Love’s Cupid

07:20.630 --> 07:23.190
Operation Love’s Cupid?

07:24.480 --> 07:26.450
Warning! Warning!

07:26.450 --> 07:28.110
Intruder in Student Council Room!

07:28.110 --> 07:32.650
Upgrading security countermeasures
from level B to A.

07:32.650 --> 07:37.040
Upgrading security countermeasures
from level A to S.

07:37.040 --> 07:39.700
Final line of defense breached.

07:39.700 --> 07:40.700
All personnel evacuate.

07:47.480 --> 07:49.480
Oh, Jesus!

07:55.940 --> 07:58.390
Did you break through the bulkheads again?

07:58.390 --> 08:03.250
Thanks to you, our security staff
keeps getting better and better.

08:03.250 --> 08:06.510
I demand an acceptable explanation, President.

08:08.400 --> 08:10.580
I thought I was being nice.

08:10.580 --> 08:13.150
This is all because of that Astral Fire

08:13.150 --> 08:14.840
you’re so attached to.

08:14.840 --> 08:16.470
Anyway, from now on,

08:16.470 --> 08:19.090
give these easy jobs to those
with more free time.

08:19.090 --> 08:22.060
Jeez... I’m busy today, too.

08:22.060 --> 08:25.980
Because you never got your answer from him?

08:32.530 --> 08:34.360
H-Hello!

08:37.160 --> 08:39.670
She got all red!

08:39.670 --> 08:41.500
Red as a beet...

08:41.500 --> 08:43.430
What’s going on here?!

08:43.910 --> 08:46.290
We wanted to ask him something.

08:46.290 --> 08:49.180
Ah, we haven’t introduced ourselves.

08:49.850 --> 08:54.830
The girl with the odd hair is my younger sister,
Vice-President Shione.

08:54.830 --> 08:57.020
“Odd” was unnecessary!

08:57.310 --> 08:59.160
Secretary Hase Anna.

08:59.160 --> 09:00.310
Hi.

09:00.560 --> 09:02.560
Treasurer Kirishima Youko.

09:02.560 --> 09:03.630
Hey.

09:04.020 --> 09:05.760
The School Beautification Head, Maruyama Yuuka.

09:05.760 --> 09:07.150
H-Hello.

09:07.770 --> 09:10.630
Out cold since Ayako’s arrival is

09:10.630 --> 09:12.570
the Executive Committee Member, Yagi Kousuke.

09:13.810 --> 09:15.350
Good luck.

09:16.600 --> 09:19.170
Oh, Fujita Mitsuki’s not here.

09:19.780 --> 09:21.300
She does the PR.

09:22.320 --> 09:24.800
And we’d like you, Yoshimura Mamoru-kun,

09:24.800 --> 09:28.910
to join the Student Council as Ayako’s aide.

09:33.580 --> 09:37.440
Wait! I just started and I don’t know anything...

09:37.440 --> 09:38.810
Don’t worry about it.

09:38.810 --> 09:41.560
You can learn on the job.

09:41.560 --> 09:43.840
What are you planning?!

09:43.840 --> 09:47.060
You aren’t telling me you’re
being nice again, are you?!

09:47.630 --> 09:48.900
Well...

09:50.190 --> 09:53.070
It just sounds like fun!

09:56.280 --> 09:59.210
All right, then...

09:59.210 --> 10:03.900
I’ll give you so much fun,
you’ll regret ever being born!

10:14.620 --> 10:16.040
That’s heavy...

10:19.310 --> 10:21.390
Another nice photo.

10:21.390 --> 10:22.900
OK... Cheese!

10:23.730 --> 10:27.040
I’ll print ’em out like always.

10:27.040 --> 10:31.370
For now, I’ll take three of the
Ayako blushing close-up.

10:31.370 --> 10:33.000
Got it.

10:33.000 --> 10:35.870
That’ll be 1200 yen per photo.

10:35.870 --> 10:38.030
That’s too expensive!

10:42.680 --> 10:44.890
Her smile, huh?

10:45.450 --> 10:48.360
<i>No one’s ever seen her smile.</i>

10:51.580 --> 10:55.380
<i>I wonder what her smile looks like.</i>

11:04.610 --> 11:06.430
G-G-Good morning...

11:06.920 --> 11:08.780
Takasu-san...

11:12.500 --> 11:16.550
Thanks so much for the ride.

11:16.550 --> 11:18.430
I-If you want,

11:18.430 --> 11:20.750
I’ll pick you up and take you home every day.

11:20.750 --> 11:22.750
No, I couldn’t.

11:22.750 --> 11:25.330
Don’t worry, Yoshimura-sama.

11:25.330 --> 11:28.200
Actually, we’d be most honored.

11:28.200 --> 11:30.950
We’ve been driving around in circles
since five this morning,

11:30.950 --> 11:33.130
so we could run into you right as you left.

11:33.880 --> 11:36.530
Kikukawa... Do you want to die?

11:36.530 --> 11:38.190
Of course not.

11:38.190 --> 11:42.550
Um, do you always go to school by car?

11:42.550 --> 11:44.070
I guess so.

11:44.070 --> 11:47.290
We can’t have her being attacked in a crowd.

11:47.290 --> 11:48.820
A-Attacked?

11:48.820 --> 11:52.620
She’s extremely popular among extremists

11:52.620 --> 11:54.940
and paramilitary organizations, all over the world.

11:54.940 --> 11:56.240
Popular?

11:56.240 --> 11:58.260
But they’re trying to kill her, right?

11:58.260 --> 11:59.620
Don’t worry.

11:59.620 --> 12:01.240
I’m strong.

12:01.600 --> 12:02.680
But still!

12:02.680 --> 12:06.130
Even if you’re strong, you’re still a girl!

12:07.740 --> 12:10.920
A girl, huh?

12:10.920 --> 12:12.570
I-It’s true, isn’t it?

12:12.570 --> 12:13.870
Got a problem with that?

12:13.870 --> 12:16.870
Not at all, of course.

12:16.870 --> 12:18.880
I would have loved to have shown

12:18.880 --> 12:22.170
Yoshimura-sama how you looked this morning.

12:22.170 --> 12:25.060
Aw, you’re kidding.

12:25.770 --> 12:28.450
He’s not...

12:34.230 --> 12:35.400
I’m getting out!

12:35.400 --> 12:37.600
Wait, Takasu-san!

12:52.410 --> 12:53.670
What is it?

12:53.670 --> 12:57.250
I asked you to follow her, and you lost her?

12:58.210 --> 13:00.250
Did you find her car?!

13:04.200 --> 13:08.000
Aya-panties this early in the morning?

13:06.090 --> 13:08.000
You idiot!

13:21.480 --> 13:23.630
I’m sorry for getting you involved in that.

13:23.630 --> 13:24.730
Are you hurt?

13:24.730 --> 13:26.910
No, I’m fine.

13:27.860 --> 13:29.450
Oh, right.

13:35.090 --> 13:38.430
Please fill out the relevant parts and submit it.

13:38.430 --> 13:41.150
This is a survey...

13:41.150 --> 13:42.880
L-Look at it later.

13:42.880 --> 13:43.890
Don’t look at it now.

13:43.890 --> 13:45.900
Anyway, I’m in a hurry!

13:45.900 --> 13:46.630
Bye!

13:49.290 --> 13:50.590
Um...

13:56.240 --> 13:58.010
Uh, next...

13:58.010 --> 14:01.270
Can I call you Mamoru?

14:01.740 --> 14:02.640
Yes.

14:03.280 --> 14:06.430
<i>Her handwriting’s so cute.</i>

14:06.430 --> 14:07.760
<i>I’m surprised.</i>

14:08.310 --> 14:10.620
OK, this is the last one...

14:13.780 --> 14:16.760
Tell me if you want to go out with me.

14:18.700 --> 14:22.460
She can’t say it face-to-face. That’s so cute!

14:22.460 --> 14:24.560
F-Fujita-san!

14:24.560 --> 14:25.790
Call me Mitsuki.

14:25.790 --> 14:27.640
Hurry, the conference is starting.

14:29.480 --> 14:32.740
Another Lab Intruder

14:30.540 --> 14:32.750
There was another intruder in the lab.

14:32.750 --> 14:36.330
And this time, the traps weren’t activated.

14:37.180 --> 14:41.810
Interesting. They saw through the traps I set.

14:42.230 --> 14:45.780
Fortunately, they couldn’t find the Astral Fire.

14:45.780 --> 14:49.100
But I think we should move it, just to be safe.

14:49.640 --> 14:54.550
This time, we’ll use the container...

14:51.910 --> 14:54.550
Um, Yuuka-san, right?

14:55.630 --> 14:56.610
Yes!

14:57.430 --> 14:58.610
What’s wrong?

14:58.610 --> 15:00.080
You look pale.

15:02.730 --> 15:05.750
No... Well, I haven’t been getting enough sleep.

15:05.750 --> 15:06.480
I see.

15:06.480 --> 15:09.030
You should eat something spicy. It’ll wake you up.

15:09.030 --> 15:11.180
S-S-S-Spy?!

15:11.180 --> 15:12.730
What’s wrong, Yuuka?

15:12.730 --> 15:13.690
Mamoru-kun?

15:13.690 --> 15:15.150
Excuse me.

15:15.150 --> 15:17.860
Nothing at all! Nothing, whatsoever!

15:18.620 --> 15:19.990
All right, then.

15:19.990 --> 15:23.620
Uh, may I ask something?

15:23.620 --> 15:25.650
What is this Astral Fire?

15:25.650 --> 15:30.760
A device that allows non-beatrice users
to use beatrice, I suppose.

15:30.760 --> 15:34.210
It was Ayako’s idea.

15:34.210 --> 15:35.930
Your idea?

15:35.930 --> 15:41.340
Yes. It’s a beatrice that’s given special orders
and placed inside a tube.

15:42.350 --> 15:43.280
But...

15:44.110 --> 15:46.890
If it fell into the hands of someone
with dangerous ideals...

15:46.890 --> 15:49.180
Wh-What would happen?

15:49.180 --> 15:54.190
Don’t worry. We’ll find the culprit.

15:55.740 --> 15:58.350
To start, we’ll set new traps.

15:59.010 --> 16:01.390
Shione, bring up the map of the lab.

16:01.390 --> 16:03.340
This is where it was held.

16:03.340 --> 16:08.680
We’ll place it with its container here,
to draw the criminal’s attention.

16:09.730 --> 16:16.070
Beatrice may be something different than I thought...

16:16.070 --> 16:19.790
I always wanted to be able to use it.

16:19.790 --> 16:21.470
When I was a kid,

16:21.470 --> 16:24.050
I was caught in an accident you
might have heard about.

16:24.510 --> 16:29.150
I was saved by a man who used beatrice.

16:29.150 --> 16:30.350
I see.

16:30.810 --> 16:35.720
But I didn’t know anyone would try to use it for evil.

16:35.720 --> 16:40.490
People try to kill you

16:40.490 --> 16:43.270
because of your ability with it, right?

16:44.830 --> 16:47.050
Shall I show you, then?

17:28.000 --> 17:29.240
A star?

17:43.860 --> 17:45.760
Takasu-san...

17:45.760 --> 17:50.340
There are a lot of different theories about beatrice.

17:50.340 --> 17:55.590
But I think you can keep trusting in
what you’ve believed in so far.

17:55.970 --> 17:56.850
OK!

17:56.850 --> 17:58.320
Thank you!

18:19.140 --> 18:22.210
Kikukawa isn’t here yet.

18:23.180 --> 18:24.610
Oh, right.

18:24.610 --> 18:25.810
Takasu-san, here you go.

18:26.730 --> 18:28.180
You filled it out already?

18:30.440 --> 18:33.990
Wow, you really wrote a lot.

18:33.990 --> 18:37.710
Sorry. I just couldn’t cut short what I wanted to say.

18:37.710 --> 18:42.850
No, I’m glad you really put some thought into it.

18:43.250 --> 18:45.800
Thanks!

18:47.000 --> 18:48.180
She smiled?

18:51.370 --> 18:53.440
No, it’s nothing...

19:00.080 --> 19:01.250
What’s this?

19:01.250 --> 19:02.310
Right.

19:02.310 --> 19:06.890
I think things like this should be said in person.

19:06.890 --> 19:12.190
S-So you’re going to answer me now...

19:14.730 --> 19:15.890
Well...

19:20.250 --> 19:22.390
I got caught in a traffic jam!

19:22.390 --> 19:23.960
Let’s go.

19:26.810 --> 19:28.010
Oh, my.

19:28.010 --> 19:29.650
Am I in the way?

19:30.350 --> 19:31.420
Yeah.

19:37.390 --> 19:38.440
What’s wrong?!

19:41.320 --> 19:43.790
Y-You’re not going to...

19:58.160 --> 20:01.310
You’ve been watching us the whole time, haven’t you?!

20:01.750 --> 20:04.580
I’m so impressed you noticed.

20:04.580 --> 20:07.140
I think you should thank me.

20:07.140 --> 20:12.940
I had a handkerchief ready for when you got shot down.

20:12.940 --> 20:14.380
Retreat, then!

20:14.380 --> 20:16.250
Aye-aye, sir!

20:19.240 --> 20:20.660
Just you wait...

20:21.030 --> 20:24.590
I’m going to shave that idiot head of yours bald!

20:24.590 --> 20:27.420
Wait!

20:27.420 --> 20:30.630
I’m so glad she’s getting along
with her fellow students...

20:40.250 --> 20:43.090
I need to give her an answer.

20:45.110 --> 20:48.190
<i>Takasu-san is really amazing...</i>

20:48.190 --> 20:51.670
<i>I don’t know why she fell in love
with someone like me.</i>

20:54.160 --> 20:56.310
<i>I’m not worthy of her.</i>

20:57.150 --> 20:59.610
<i>The more I learn, the more I hesitate.</i>

21:00.720 --> 21:03.110
<i>But...</i>

21:03.110 --> 21:08.650
<i>But why do I want to know more about her?</i>

21:21.120 --> 21:23.060
Yes, Yoshimura residence...

21:23.060 --> 21:24.330
Is that you, Mamoru-kun?

21:24.330 --> 21:26.780
I’m sorry for calling so early.

21:26.780 --> 21:29.350
Is that you, Student Council President?

21:29.350 --> 21:32.890
I’m sorry to ask this, but can you come to school?

21:32.890 --> 21:35.780
You see, the world’s in danger.

21:35.780 --> 21:39.270
Oh, I see. The world’s in...

21:39.270 --> 21:41.390
The world’s in danger?!

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:17.290 --> 23:18.740
I may not know what’s coming tomorrow,

23:18.740 --> 23:20.500
but when it gets down to it, I’m ready for anything!

23:20.500 --> 23:22.510
It’s a valuable treasure, and we won’t let them have it!

23:22.510 --> 23:25.520
And a couple’s passion alights in an abandoned building!

23:25.520 --> 23:27.460
Or so I’m told...

23:27.460 --> 23:31.480
You can’t tell what’s actually going to happen from that?

23:31.480 --> 23:33.480
Y-Yeah, that makes sense.

23:33.480 --> 23:38.500
